{title: 444 - I'm a Pilgrim}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Early Advent}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]I’m a pilgrim, and I’m a [C]stranger;
I can [F]tarry, I can [C]tarry [C7]but a [F]night;
Do not de[C]tain me, for I am [F]going
To where the [C]fountains are [G]ever [C]flowing.
[F]I’m a pilgrim, and I’m a [C]stranger;
I can [F]tarry, I can [C]tarry [C7]but a [F]night.

Refrain:
[F]I'm a pilgrim, [C]and I'm a stranger;
[F]I can [C]tarry, I [C7]can tarry [F]but a night.

Verse 2:
[F]There the glory [C]is ever shining!
[F]O, my [C]longing heart, [C7]my longing [F]heart is there;
[C]Here in this country [F]so dark and dreary,
[C]I long [G]have wandered [C]forlorn and weary.

Verse 3:
[F]There's the city [C]to which I journey;
[F]My [C]Redeemer, my [C7]Redeemer is [F]its light!
[C]There is no [F]sorrow, nor any sighing,
[C]Nor any [G]tears there, [C]or any dying.
